1320
00:49:29.139 --> 00:49:31.126
And then also a few introductory movements,

1321
00:49:31.126 --> 00:49:33.630
probably another hour worth of videos we made.

1322
00:49:33.630 --> 00:49:35.159
And I suspect there's gotta be a ton on YouTube.

1323
00:49:35.159 --> 00:49:35.992
Right.

1324
00:49:35.992 --> 00:49:39.925
It's the kind of thing where I hate to say it,

1325
00:49:39.925 --> 00:49:41.539
but I do think at least initially,

1326
00:49:41.539 --> 00:49:43.622
you do need an instructor

1327
00:49:44.587 --> 00:49:45.568
because at least for me,

1328
00:49:45.568 --> 00:49:47.760
and I think I have decent proprioception in kinesthetic

1329
00:49:47.760 --> 00:49:50.901
awareness, not amazing, but good.

1330
00:49:50.901 --> 00:49:51.997
I don't think I could have done it

1331
00:49:51.997 --> 00:49:56.531
without somebody there to poke and prod and correct.

1332
00:49:56.531 --> 00:49:59.441
And even today, like I just,

1333
00:49:59.441 --> 00:50:01.084
I get more out of it when Kyle's there.

1334
00:50:01.084 --> 00:50:02.419
And even when he's there,

1335
00:50:02.419 --> 00:50:04.378
he's filming me to this day.

1336
00:50:04.378 --> 00:50:05.572
Filming and commenting,

1337
00:50:05.572 --> 00:50:06.617
so that when I'm doing it on my own,

1338
00:50:06.617 --> 00:50:10.721
I'm watching a video and I'm listening to his cue.

1339
00:50:10.721 --> 00:50:13.366
And would you say that that is foundational

1340
00:50:13.366 --> 00:50:17.299
and a kind of requisite prior to the work

1341
00:50:17.299 --> 00:50:19.644
that you do with Beth?

1342
